{
  "_about": "Overlay-at-anchor sprites (js/shared/overlay.js; spec in docs/shared-api.md s5). bases: a sprite (img, its pixel size) with named anchors as normalised [x, y] in the image, a greybox shape for when there's no image, and fit: per-layer nudges {dx, dy, w} (fractions of the base) so each overlay sits within 4 px on this base. layers: an overlay drawn with its pivot (0..1 of its own box) on an anchor, w a fraction of the drawn base width, aspect h/w (or size [w, h] of its image), z order (base is 0; negative goes behind), tint true = a neutral sprite coloured in code, slot = what it replaces when worn (Dress up's slots: head, top, layer, bottom, feet, wrap, wrist, carry), shape = its greybox. 'item:*' is the template for any held item: item:<word id> takes its picture from the mode (opts.itemImage). Anchors on the three upper-body crops are measured by eye from assets/cook/characters/*-neutral.webp (the crops end at the chest, so 'hands' sits on the bottom edge: a held item is shown held up in front); tune them in lab/shared.html. colours: placeholder hexes for code tints until the family's colour words arrive (Dress up's colour words carry their own hex, which wins).",
